---
import DocsLayout from "../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Callout from "../../../components/Callout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Kubernetes">
  <h1>Kubernetes</h1>
  <p>Identity is stateless and runs comfortably as a Deployment with two ports. The example below assumes you already have an EntDB Service running in the same namespace.</p>

  <h2>Secrets</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: identity-secrets
  namespace: identity
type: Opaque
stringData:
  # JWT key ring (see docs/installation/jwt-keys)
  GATEWAY_JWT_KEYS: |
    [
      {
        "kid": "k1",
        "private_key_pem": "-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n",
        "active": true
      }
    ]
  # 32-byte base64 key for AES-GCM-encrypting TOTP secrets
  GATEWAY_TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY: "<openssl rand -base64 32>"
  # OAuth (only if you use it)
  GATEWAY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: ""
  GATEWAY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET: ""
  GATEWAY_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID: ""
  GATEWAY_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET: ""</code></pre>

  <h2>ConfigMap</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: identity-config
  namespace: identity
data:
  GATEWAY_ENTDB_ADDRESS: "entdb.entdb.svc.cluster.local:50051"
  GATEWAY_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID: "my-product"
  GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_ID: "app.my-product.com"
  GATEWAY_PASSKEY_RP_NAME: "My Product"
  GATEWAY_PASSKEY_ORIGIN: "https://app.my-product.com"
  GATEWAY_TOTP_ISSUER: "My Product"
  GATEWAY_DEFAULT_EMAIL_DOMAIN: "my-product.com"
  GATEWAY_ALLOWED_ORIGINS: "https://app.my-product.com,https://admin.my-product.com"
  GATEWAY_COOKIE_SECURE: "true"
  GATEWAY_AUTH_ALLOW_LOCAL: "true"</code></pre>

  <h2>Deployment</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: identity
  namespace: identity
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels: { app: identity }
  template:
    metadata:
      labels: { app: identity }
    spec:
      securityContext:
        runAsNonRoot: true
        runAsUser: 65532
        seccompProfile: { type: RuntimeDefault }
      containers:
        - name: identity
          image: ghcr.io/elloloop/identity:0.1.0
          ports:
            - { name: http,    containerPort: 80 }
            - { name: metrics, containerPort: 9090 }
          envFrom:
            - configMapRef: { name: identity-config }
            - secretRef:    { name: identity-secrets }
          livenessProbe:
            httpGet: { path: /health, port: http }
            initialDelaySeconds: 5
            periodSeconds: 10
          readinessProbe:
            httpGet: { path: /health, port: http }
            initialDelaySeconds: 2
            periodSeconds: 5
          resources:
            requests: { cpu: 100m, memory: 128Mi }
            limits:   { cpu: 500m, memory: 512Mi }
          securityContext:
            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
            capabilities: { drop: ["ALL"] }</code></pre>

  <h2>Service</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: identity
  namespace: identity
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector: { app: identity }
  ports:
    - { name: http,    port: 80,   targetPort: http }
    - { name: metrics, port: 9090, targetPort: metrics }</code></pre>

  <h2>Ingress (example with cert-manager)</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: Ingress
metadata:
  name: identity
  namespace: identity
  annotations:
    cert-manager.io/cluster-issuer: letsencrypt-prod
spec:
  tls:
    - hosts: [identity.my-product.com]
      secretName: identity-tls
  rules:
    - host: identity.my-product.com
      http:
        paths:
          - path: /
            pathType: Prefix
            backend:
              service: { name: identity, port: { number: 80 } }</code></pre>

  <Callout type="info" title="Replicas are safe">
    Identity holds no per-instance state &mdash; refresh tokens, sessions, TOTP secrets, and challenges all live in EntDB. Run as many replicas as you like; downstream services don't care which replica issued a token because they verify locally via JWKS.
  </Callout>

  <h2>ServiceMonitor (Prometheus Operator)</h2>
  <pre is:raw><code class="language-yaml">apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: identity
  namespace: identity
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels: { app: identity }
  endpoints:
    - port: metrics
      interval: 30s</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
